• Adding the scroll-not-squeeze rules to the table CSS in `index.html`.

• Done.

  - Added `.table-wrap > table { min-width: 720px; }` — every table now scrolls inside its `.table-wrap` (which already had `overflow-x: auto`) instead of squeezing; `width: 100%` still lets it fill wider containers.
  - Added `td:not(.nw) { min-width: 18ch; }` — long-text cells (model, role, output, title, evidence, boundary, owner, next_input, value) keep a readable floor and wrap normally; short cells already carry `nw: true` in the render code and stay `white-space: nowrap` via the existing `.nw` rule.
  - No other rules touched; page-level overflow unchanged (table min-width lives inside the scrolling container, so body scrollWidth stays equal to clientWidth).

  Final size of `index.html`: 11,635 bytes.

